/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ethylChloride-toluene -- A HENRY'S-LAW CONSTANT FROM EVERY LABORATORY'S MEASUREMENTS.

  WRITTEN BY bin/curate/henry_organic.py declare (DEV.md 4c C321 part 2).

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (the
  declarations of the run share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  Solute ethylChloride (CAS 75-00-3) in solvent toluene (CAS 108-88-3),
  joined to the archive by InChIKey through identity.json -- never by name.
  The solute is the compound the block's Henry property names.
  CLASS: ethylChloride: Tb 285.42 K, Tc 460.3 K; toluene: Tb 383.78 K, Tc 591.75 K.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/henryArchiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, block, extract sha256);
  `bin/curate/henry_organic.py fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every mole-fraction-scale Henry block of the pair with a stated
  uncertainty on every point (1 block(s)).  FITTED, ALL OF THEM:
      10.1021/je060395n              block 123   5 pts  250.04-329.99 K   Miyano, Y.[Yoshimori]; Kimura, A.[Arisa]; Kuroda, M.[Mikiko] et al. (2007) J. Chem. Eng. Data 52, 291-297, doi:10.1021/je060395n

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C283 amended, C285, C300; C321 part 2).  The van't Hoff
  form the loader reads, ln H = ln H_ref + (enthalpy/R)(1/T - 1/298.15 K):
  two parameters.  Stage 1, least squares on the relative residual
  H_model/H - 1 (equal weights); a point above 20 % is DISCARDED BY NAME and
  stage 1 repeated -- ONLY when two or more laboratories are fitted: with ONE
  laboratory no point is discarded (no second series to call it an outlier
  against; C321 part 2 amended) and the grade is the series' real error.  Stage 2, minimax on
  the same residual over the kept points; its coefficients are the record's.  GRADE on the max relative
  error over the kept points: clean up to 5 %, warning up to 10 %, severe up
  to 20 %, refused above.  An in-sample clean resting on ONE laboratory is
  capped at warning (C300 rule 2).  One temperature gives no enthalpy: refused.
  clean and warning are promoted (autoPromoted, review by none) into
  data/standards/parameters/Henry/; severe stays in this case's
  constant/parameters/Henry/ (C300 rule 3); refused writes nothing.

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  5 points of 1 laboratory(ies); 5 kept,
  0 discarded after the least-squares stage (> 20 %):
  ONE laboratory: no point was discarded (C321 part 2 amended).
  H_ref = 1.51338e+05 Pa at 298.15 K, enthalpy = -25833 J/mol;
  kept span 250.04-329.99 K; max relative error
  1.8845 % (least squares 2.2795 %); in-sample
  grade clean, CAPPED to warning (singleLaboratory).
  PROMOTED into data/standards/parameters/Henry/.
  @@RESULT-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The constant is the infinite-dilution H_xp at the
  solvent's own vapour pressure, in the measured range only; the archive's
  transcription has NOT been read back against the articles.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    { name h_ethylChloride_toluene; type pairLookup; components ( ethylChloride toluene ); }
);
